[{"id":"VRCE-1-24-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing this excellent speech of that ascetic of immeasurable energy, that foremost of men answered him in these happy words,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4851226670ee4f4ee69c3fa223856b4e217b619440e745f20cdd9e24238a550","compact":"924e06ef29eb83bd84001d31294689018b4f72886410c41f33361d52424322fd","nasal":"924e06ef29eb83bd84001d31294689018b4f72886410c41f33361d52424322fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":2,"english":"O best of ascetics, I have heard that the Yakşa race is endowed with but small prowess. How can then that one of the weaker sex possess the strength of a thousand elephants?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.466,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"745b4063bf4c3d99e5dad83500904ae1298599e58a3beb036dbbe68bb7fc4040","compact":"b93a10ab08d8a360a5644ed0c43c00c3c8b758a957b823d7a94df99d6ea4575b","nasal":"8096915ee5878319b3af7334daeb714eb7ece03c32697f6d40c71f219f1cfde3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":3,"english":"Hearing this speech that was uttered by Rāghava of immeasurable energy, Viśvāmitra, delighting with his amiable words that subduer of foes, Rāma, and Laksmana, said, Do you listen as to the means whereby attaining terrible strength, that one belonging to the weaker sex has come to possess strength and prowess by virtue of a boon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4463ef1aedc418af24f916e42e1f3718fdcb33c2b81f378c9b0fabc921a3180","compact":"18f61efce135bac4ecdd179794f71b3ccbf948ce4ee3f93752078562f7fdd08b","nasal":"18f61efce135bac4ecdd179794f71b3ccbf948ce4ee3f93752078562f7fdd08b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":4,"english":"In former times there was a mighty and exceedingly powerful Yaksa, named Suketu. And he had no issue. And he was of pure practices, and used to perform rigid austerities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a871bee515164a34c6ca3a6197f5e61df3d185452024d93382cd36a9db4aaa11","compact":"2892c07184a7e05f75d01846e9b5f1aca401b448754b4bead57cf14762cf5b37","nasal":"2892c07184a7e05f75d01846e9b5f1aca401b448754b4bead57cf14762cf5b37"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":5,"english":"And, O Rāma, the Grand-sire endowed her with that lord of Yakşas, conferred upon him a gem of a daughter, by name Tāțakā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bdda2a078d379e3b462555fee6640067e1ef9c23ff53b04c07e9f5f8c962d186","compact":"7353128c646d60d948e927db6593e228e21bf2c8476bd995df2827453afa9025","nasal":"7353128c646d60d948e927db6593e228e21bf2c8476bd995df2827453afa9025"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":6,"english":"And the Grand-sire endowed her with the strength of a thousand elephants; yet that illustrious one did not bestow a son on that Yaksa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.763,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eb225b80a9e5cabcaa7ad157ca18acbf61ef4b83ff1724e9c874a559b925760e","compact":"802c3f4b9bd11e1dfaa49d1f711855517f6b4248f75af2e126d74a5e9c96517b","nasal":"802c3f4b9bd11e1dfaa49d1f711855517f6b4248f75af2e126d74a5e9c96517b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":7,"english":"When she had grown, and attained youth and beauty, he gave that famous damsel to Jambha's son, Sunda, for wife.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.731,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e141fe8d29ed7eb449204a0534ad19d3eb0a767315745a5138515f2c44c632c0","compact":"5c0c7d1cf49ba8ebcf4e8a846212e34709407621d00c5570a7ca947f102c5ecd","nasal":"bcb26cfa9dd01c17414db631d1dcf757095ca218f165dd008947b4d7de2e37d1"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":8,"english":"After a length of time, that Yakṣī gave birth to a son, named Mārīca, possessed of irrepressible energy, him who became a Rākṣasa in consequence of a curse.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0ee5362d9946f3aa3db855acc01df419b7a5a5c6538829afc66020d9c8587a39","compact":"ac24cb7a7ab7c80b3591facd124d78a963c69bf39620fe512b9390e266a4cb97","nasal":"ac24cb7a7ab7c80b3591facd124d78a963c69bf39620fe512b9390e266a4cb97"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":9,"english":"O Rāma, when Sunda had been destroyed, Tat akā along with her son, set her heart upon afflicting that excellent saint Agastya.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b0f2cb4c9b5f1f39256a5b5fa06d4da04d208d31fb40c719a7d4805299e686fb","compact":"a3e0af0ecafae06ea666c690d372cb983163183a76f89910767dcf16a6ec5ed1","nasal":"d742f42431ff3ef7ee1a00a5eb77478d8b2e0a861d0dca08bc08cc8246f0147e"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":10,"english":"And enraged with Agastya, she rushed at him with a roar, intending to devour him. And on seeing her thus rushing, that worshipful saint, Agastya, said to Mārīca, Do you become a Raksasa! .","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.429,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"03c51859c49a9e9617019b2f328a01f9eb30d9eeabb3a056e9c1497eaa470850","compact":"465d879350c561a4e49e4fc0f430f78c3f4b025602f51e2a455f2b6934cab975","nasal":"465d879350c561a4e49e4fc0f430f78c3f4b025602f51e2a455f2b6934cab975"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":11,"english":"And, in exceeding wrath, he also cursed Tataka. And, O mighty Yaksi, since in frightful guise with a frightful face you have desired to eat up a human being, do you immediately leave this (your original) shape, and become of a terrible form!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.569,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1e4aa021e8c734aa7c4228e32a3af8df4e9a1cad73d4270301e066c2fe263f3d","compact":"cd228888792fd22ddf7bcfd3fbe9a6141616c7fcf87c6df20c51f10dc27c5938","nasal":"cd228888792fd22ddf7bcfd3fbe9a6141616c7fcf87c6df20c51f10dc27c5938"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":12,"english":"Thus cursed by Agastya, Tățakā, overwhelmed with rage, lays waste this fair region, where Agastya carry on his austerities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3bc2bef328b15d96781c513d3c4886a6f1d29ef515625ec369775955d177ff1d","compact":"a2377ecf8143fef199b52340ec588c761e3524dbd6799093559b627d48cea12b","nasal":"a2377ecf8143fef199b52340ec588c761e3524dbd6799093559b627d48cea12b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":13,"english":"Do you, O descendant of Raghu, for the welfare of Brāhmaṇas and kine, slay this exceedingly terrible Yakṣī of wicked ways and vile prowess!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ff58524b612aa595f0e655fb7c25cdd28d65da597a86c14985bf05b061adabf","compact":"53d2b9ef3b90a4dbdbc939260cdcdb222a5cf96ddedeac3652e32c7c8a4e63fc","nasal":"53d2b9ef3b90a4dbdbc939260cdcdb222a5cf96ddedeac3652e32c7c8a4e63fc"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":14,"english":"Nor, O son of Raghu, does any one in the three worlds, save, you, dare to slay this Yaksi joined with a curse.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1114b900c3e1c1b8ab457233ce8a7d6b04089ff7e967e91651f492bad9c6681c","compact":"fb5e7f1fd7198df41b016e719487639c7061ccaec9f7ba28a724568b10baea1f","nasal":"5d3c51c5fb7cac10e4cf0b64819ba65372fafad2d646d00f0658ac41095d67dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":15,"english":"Nor should you, O best of men, shrink from slaying a woman; for even this should be accomplished by a prince in the interests of the four orders.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d0af94e47e245da40e7bae60240ac9d72290ceb4d5de4f35fac0b051ca249d98","compact":"be7a95c8f65632c0b3a8e4101a4068aeeafade6210594ad06e7686ab22cbe6ca","nasal":"be7a95c8f65632c0b3a8e4101a4068aeeafade6210594ad06e7686ab22cbe6ca"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":16,"english":"Of those engaged in the onerous task of government, even this is the eternal rule of conduct. Do you, O Kākutstha, slay this impious one; for she know no righteousness!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.561,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9de8a9162bfadbb27e3c2596c020d3bb92d421e470362477150f2a2134ea1190","compact":"86aec6bc7fda33889d28625f826104d3b474e46c6901fd82bfa588f065ecc94d","nasal":"86aec6bc7fda33889d28625f826104d3b474e46c6901fd82bfa588f065ecc94d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":17,"english":"We hear, O king, that in days of yore, ſakra slew Virocana's daughter, Mantharā, who had intended to destroy the earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"489eb66299adf19591782527ce8ffff3c09e9ffd2de92bd535a6e844fb9122d2","compact":"852bba6e20ca62e5c00bddc033d7cc1c04d04ef484949127e41956a30e4bf0fd","nasal":"59152104be3474322d1d21d7649889301e7c831d3f4c2f55ba4b98ae9174cba5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":18,"english":"And formerly, O Rama, Visnu destroyed Kāvya's mother, the devoted wife of Bhrgu, who had set her heart upon annihilating the world, deprived of sleep (through fear of her.)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.844,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8daddb2a1c2a04bb28d8782a6ca986388c3be976c98451d6ba3d5c180edc149c","compact":"82b3019a3df4b1c1dee7a428f6e207578c10fd6e32fd384893810bab7d29be76","nasal":"82cdb0de9fb7303aaef009790f058e6a7a22c9fa64aa92a250042e9d624aec7b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-24-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":24,"verse":19,"english":"By these as well as innumerable princesforemost of men have wicked women been slain. Therefore, O king, renouncing antipathy, do you, by my command, slay this one!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.721,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-25-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1024019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"128596ed46e05255331388e4b58972a4390c6bd7e4e96299b3ce7ee8ffec952f","compact":"f52298574ebae422fc73c36a1d8a5724820ba81fcd19696acfa365042fed8590","nasal":"f52298574ebae422fc73c36a1d8a5724820ba81fcd19696acfa365042fed8590"}}]
